.TH PROXIMO 1 "October 2026" "proximo 0.45.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
proximo \- Model Context Protocol server for the Proxmox products
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B proximo
.br
.B proximo
.BR mint | doctor | badge | arm | disarm
.RI [ ARGS ]
.br
.B proximo \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B proximo
is a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server for Proxmox VE, Proxmox Backup
Server, Proxmox Mail Gateway and Proxmox Datacenter Manager. It serves six
tools (\fBproximo_find\fR, \fBproximo_plan\fR, \fBproximo_read\fR,
\fBproximo_call\fR, \fBaudit_entries\fR, \fBaudit_verify\fR) over every
REST address those products publish, using the vendor's own API token. An
in-container command edge (\fBssh\fR to the host, then \fBpct exec\fR) and
an in-guest QEMU guest-agent edge are off by default.
.PP
.B proximo
speaks MCP over standard input/output. It is meant to be launched on
demand by an MCP client, not started as a daemon or run interactively.
With no arguments it starts the stdio server and blocks until the client
closes the stream. The same install ships \fBproximo-core\fR, the shell
door to the same engine, and the optional network doors
\fBproximo-mcp-http\fR, \fBproximo-http\fR and \fBproximo-a2a\fR.
.PP
Every call passes one seam, the same for every door:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
.B PLAN
: a mutation without confirmation returns its verdict and the target as
it stands, and changes nothing. A mutation runs only when the operator is
armed and the address carries an authored blast-radius tier.
.IP \(bu 2
.B CONSENT
: off until \fBPROXIMO_CONSENT_DIR\fR is set; then a mutation needs a
per-plan consent id.
.IP \(bu 2
.B PROVE
: a hash-chained, HMAC-keyed audit ledger records every call. It is keyed
always; \fBaudit_verify\fR walks the chain.
.IP \(bu 2
.B UNDO
: on by default (\fBPROXIMO_UNDO\fR); a mutation with a published read at
the same address captures the record first, so the vendor's own write can
put it back.
.IP \(bu 2
.B DIAGNOSE
: read-only batteries of the vendor's own reads.
.IP \(bu 2
.B CONTAIN
: a trip file (\fBPROXIMO_CONTAIN_TRIP_PATH\fR), a rate cap
(\fBPROXIMO_RATE_MAX\fR), a forbid list (\fBPROXIMO_FORBID\fR) and taint
tracking on content a guest or a stranger wrote.
.RE
.PP
SCOPE and LEASE belong to the Proxmox token itself: its ACL and its
\fBexpire\fR. \fBproximo mint\fR prints the vendor's commands to make that
token. A set \fBPROXIMO_SCOPE_PATH\fR, or a \fBPROXIMO_ARM_TTL\fR above 0,
stops every door at start and names what to set instead.
.SH THE OPERATOR'S VERBS
The verbs run on the shell door, the same as \fBproximo-core\fR \fIverb\fR.
.TP
.B proximo doctor
Read-only: the gate diagnoses itself. It reads the record, each configured
plane (the vendor's own \fBGET /version\fR and \fBGET
/access/permissions\fR, run and receipted like any read), the ledger's
chain, and which of the six pillars stand, with the one line that would
raise an empty one. Takes no arguments; prints one JSON report. It reports
that a switch is set, never where it points.
.TP
.B proximo mint \fIPLANE\fR
Prints the vendor's commands to make the write token, bounded by its own
ACL and expiry. Runs nothing.
.TP
.B proximo arm\fR | \fBdisarm
Grant or withdraw write authority for this operator.
.TP
.B proximo badge
Mint or inspect a caller badge for the network doors.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Proximo is configured entirely through environment variables; there is no
separate configuration-file syntax of its own (see \fBFILES\fR below for
the optional \fIproximo.env\fR loader). This section lists only the
handful of variables needed to get started \(em it is deliberately not a
full reference; see \fBFILES\fR for where the complete list lives.
.PP
Required for the default single-target setup:
.TP
.B PROXIMO_API_BASE_URL
Proxmox VE API base URL, e.g. \fIhttps://pve.example.lan:8006/api2/json\fR.
.TP
.B PROXIMO_TOKEN_PATH
Path to a file containing exactly \fIUSER@REALM!TOKENID=SECRET\fR. The
file is read at call time, not held in memory at rest; never pass the
token itself as an inline environment value.
.PP
Notable safety toggles, both off by default:
.TP
.B PROXIMO_ENABLE_EXEC
Turns on the in-container exec edge (\fBssh\fR \(-> \fBpct exec\fR), gated
by the fail-closed \fBPROXIMO_CT_ALLOWLIST\fR.
.TP
.B PROXIMO_ENABLE_AGENT
Turns on the in-guest QEMU guest-agent edge, gated by the fail-closed
\fBPROXIMO_AGENT_ALLOWLIST\fR.
.PP
The complete \fBPROXIMO_*\fR reference \(em every variable, every plane
(PVE/PBS/PMG/PDM), the opt-in trust-spine extensions, and multi-target
registries \(em is documented in \fI/usr/share/doc/proximo/proximo.env.example\fR
and in the upstream README (see \fBSEE ALSO\fR).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/proximo/proximo.env
Optional. Sourced once at process start; fills only \fBPROXIMO_*\fR names
that are not already set in the real environment (real/inline environment
always wins). Override the path with \fBPROXIMO_ENV_FILE\fR. This exists
so an MCP client's inline \fIenv\fR block and a file-based configuration
behave the same way.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/proximo/proximo.env.example
The complete, annotated \fBPROXIMO_*\fR environment variable reference,
shipped with this package.
.TP
.I /opt/venvs/proximo/
The self-contained Python virtual environment bundling proximo and its
runtime dependencies (\fImcp\fR, \fIhttpx\fR). \fI/usr/bin/proximo\fR is a
symlink into it. Not meant to be activated or modified directly.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal exit: the MCP client closed the stdio stream, \fB\-\-help\fR, or
\fBdoctor\fR ran whole.
.TP
.B 3
Refused at start: an unknown argument, a retired switch still set
(\fBPROXIMO_SURFACES\fR, \fBPROXIMO_SCOPE_PATH\fR, \fBPROXIMO_ARM_TTL\fR),
or a configuration the server cannot build from. For \fBdoctor\fR, nothing
is configured. A short message goes to standard error.
.TP
.B 4
\fBdoctor\fR only: a configured plane is unreachable, or the ledger's chain
cannot be judged.
.SH SEE ALSO
Full documentation, the complete environment variable reference, and the
trust-spine design: \fIhttps://github.com/john-broadway/proximo\fR
.PP
.I /usr/share/doc/proximo/README.Debian
